{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Stage Docker Build.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Stage Docker Build.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multi stage docker build multi stage docker build","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Stage Docker Build.md","fileName":"Multi-Stage Docker Build.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multi-Stage Docker Build","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 11:23\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Containerized Microservice Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Containerized Microservice Architecture","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Stage Docker Build.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Stage Docker Build.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"multi stage docker build multi stage docker build","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Stage Docker Build.md","fileName":"Multi-Stage Docker Build.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Multi-Stage Docker Build","heading":"Multi-Stage Docker Build","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A multi-stage Docker build uses one image with the .NET SDK to restore, compile, test, and publish an application, then copies only the published output into a separate runtime image. Build tools and intermediate files do not become part of the deployed container.\n\nThe result is smaller and has a narrower attack surface while retaining a reproducible build recipe. Stage ordering also affects cache reuse, so stable dependency inputs are commonly copied before frequently changing source files.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Containerized Microservice Architecture","hands-onrestfulwebserviceswithaspnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Multi-Stage Docker Build.md::2","sourc